// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rules/runtime/ - the model against an external store. Copy this file, rename it, delete this
// header.
//
//   Name it  <Topic>Rules.cs  and name the class the same: LiveRules.cs holds LiveRules.
//
//   Rename to `.cs`. A `.template` file is not scanned, which is the only reason this one can sit
//   here without the run trying to execute it.
//
// When it runs   Last, one file at a time in tier order, and only this folder can be skipped -
//                `--skip-runtime-validation` leaves it out and records that it did.
//
// What you get   IRuntimeContext: everything rules/global/ has, plus the two this folder exists
//                for -
//
//                context.Db("name")      read-only SQL. Column<T>(sql), Set<T>(sql),
//                                        Scalar<T>(sql), Rows(sql)
//                context.Redis("name")   read-only. Get(key), Field(key, field)
//
//                They are on this type and on no other, which is what makes the skip switch mean
//                something: a rule needing a store cannot be sitting in another folder.
//
//                The names come from the recipe's Validation.Connections, which is also where
//                `${ENV_VAR}` in a connection string is resolved.
//
// Read only      Statements that are not queries are refused, but treat that as a convenience
//                rather than the boundary. **The boundary is a read-only account.**
//
//                These rules hold a connection while they run, which is why the folder is
//                sequential: twenty of them at once is a load test against somebody's database.
//
// Priority       [RulePriority(-10)] on the class puts it in an earlier tier - see rules/global/.
//
// This folder is flat. A file one level down is not run at all; put shared helpers in
// rules/shared/.
//
// Full guide: doc/validation.md
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

